msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_1"
msgstr ""
"Echo tanks under blue skies. I did everything to prevent this from "
"happening. Yet here we are."

msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_2"
msgstr ""
"Press a button, and they come running here like rats. And they have no "
"choice."

msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_3"
msgstr ""
"Once you learn their patterns, a battle becomes a hunt. You play by their "
"rules, you lose. Set your own rules? Victory's in the bag."

msgid "meta/shortStory/ls_artefact_4"
msgstr ""
"Mirror Phase trials completed with full success. The Phase remains stable "
"and securely isolated from our dimension."

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_1"
msgstr ""
"Echo tanks under blue skies. I did everything to prevent this from "
"happening. Yet here we are.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}There's "
"something surreal about engaging these monstrosities in broad daylight. No "
"fog, no darkness, no eerie mist—just dazzling sunshine gleaming on their "
"twisted metal.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}The strangest part? Without "
"all that gloom, I feel stronger. More focused. That gnawing fear that used "
"to crawl up my spine is gone, replaced by something more primal. More "
"electric.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}It's pure adrenaline now. And "
"damn, it feels good.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Come on, "
"{violet_open}Pied Piper{violet_close}—work those fingers, play your tune. "
"Lead a new batch to us."

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_2"
msgstr ""
"You know what's beautiful? We can finally control these bastards—to an "
"extent, at least.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}This "
"{violet_open}Wavebreaker{violet_close} device we've rigged up is something "
"else. When we activate it, the echo tanks go completely berserk. Press a "
"button, and they come running here like rats. And they have no choice. "
"They'll do anything to destroy the source of the "
"signal.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}The operator we named "
"{violet_open}\"Pied Piper\"{violet_close} is a strange one. Where the "
"command finds these types, I'll never know. This one's definitely been in "
"the anomaly. Seems a bit cracked in the head. But he knows his business. "
"It's like he can feel those things. The way he works that device, he's not "
"operating it—he's playing it like some kind of musical instrument. Gives me "
"the creeps watching his fingers dance across those "
"controls.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}He sets the required settings, and"
" we decide ourselves how the battle unfolds: the frequency of waves, as well"
" as the number and even the types of enemy "
"vehicles.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}The tables have turned. We're "
"fighting on our terms now. No more reacting to threats. No more trying to "
"survive. We're the hunters, and they're running straight into our "
"crosshairs.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}I could get used to this."

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_3"
msgstr ""
"What we're doing here isn't just warfare anymore—it's a safari. Dangerous, "
"sure, but calculated. Controlled. We know exactly what we're dealing with "
"now.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Once you learn their patterns, a battle"
" becomes a hunt. You play by their rules, you lose. Set your own rules? "
"Victory's in the bag.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}We've got the best of "
"the best here. This stuff is definitely not for newbies. But the enemy is "
"still dangerous.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}The crews size each other "
"up after each engagement—comparing kills, watching each other's tactics. And"
" that way, we get healthy competition.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Each "
"of us wants to prove their worth, show what they're made "
"of.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Just a bit longer and our trials will be"
" complete. The command will be impressed with the results, that's for sure. "
"Echo tanks don't stand a chance against us anymore. Nobody does."

msgid "meta/story/ls_artefact_4"
msgstr ""
"{header_open}CAPTAIN SMITH'S REPORT{header_close}\n"
"{header_open}TOP SECRET{header_close}{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Mirror Phase trials completed with full success. The Phase remains stable and securely isolated from our dimension. The {violet_open}Wavebreaker{violet_close} functions exactly as calculated. Technical data obtained from the Architect's satellite has been fully validated in practice.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Personnel demonstrate increased efficiency in Mirror Phase conditions. The absence of most stress factors allows crews to focus entirely on tactical aspects of battling echo tanks.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}However, I must express my concern regarding the plans to build similar {violet_open}Wavebreaker{violet_close} complexes in other regions. I question the necessity of such measures. The existing complex possesses all required infrastructure and can be scaled up to train additional crews.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}I would also like to address information about the planned construction of observation platforms with premium zones for high-ranking officers and special observers. Despite the relative safety of operations in the Mirror Phase, I consider such measures inappropriate. Combat training is not a spectacle for entertaining guests, regardless of their rank.{paragraph_open}{paragraph_close}Sincerely,\n"
"Captain Smith"

